# docs/images/

This directory is **not** the public docs site.

| Path | Audience | What belongs here |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `docs/en/`, `docs/zh/` | Public VitePress site (`docs.openviking.net` / `docs.openviking.ai`) | Full product docs: self-hosted, local, and cloud |
| `docs/images/agents/` | Volcengine OpenViking **console** (cloud / server-mode) | Short setup for connecting an agent to the managed endpoint |

`docs/images/` also holds static assets (logos, GIFs, screenshots) that README and the console hotlink. The agent markdown under `docs/images/agents/{en,zh}/` is a separate, shorter copy of the install guides.

## Rules for `docs/images/agents/`

- Assume the user already has an OpenViking Service instance on Volcengine.
- Default the endpoint to `https://api.vikingdb.cn-beijing.volces.com/openviking`.
- Prefer the TOS installer: `https://ovrelease.tos-cn-beijing.volces.com/memory-plugin-shared/install.sh --dist tos`.
- Tell them to pick **Volcengine OpenViking Cloud** / **OpenViking Service (VolcEngine Cloud)** and paste the API key from the console page.
- Do not copy the full site guides (self-hosted init, local Python env, long design notes).
- Do not treat `docs/en/` or `docs/zh/` as the source of truth for this folder, or the other way around. Update both trees when install commands change, but keep the console copy shorter and cloud-only.

Hermes is built-in: `hermes memory setup openviking` → keep **OpenViking Service (VolcEngine Cloud)** → paste API key. There is no plugin and no Base URL to type.
